12.We hasten to add that the directions aforesaid shall not only apply to the cases under Section 498-A of the I.P.C. or Section 4 of the Dowry Prohibition Act, the case in hand, but also such cases where offence is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may be less than seven years or Yallanti Supriya vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 2 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/96221108/
6 which may extend to seven years; whether with or without fine.
10.
The petitioners are obliged to render their fullest cooperation in the ongoing investigation.
12. In the result, the Criminal Petition is disposed of directing the Investigating Officer to comply with Section 35(3) of 'the BNSS'/41-A of 'the Cr.P.C.,' and to strictly follow the directions issued in the cases of Satender Kumar Antil, Arnesh Kumar and MD. Asfak Alam.
As a sequel, Miscellaneous petitions, if any pending, shall stand closed.

